# StreamVersion 1.2
# The file named on the command line does not exist, so the viewer opens on the drop zone with a
# "file not found" message. Its "Open file..." action (the dialog is answered by
# CTEST_OPEN_DIALOG_FILE) then loads a model, and the frame left on screen has to show it. The action
# reaches the event loop through the notification center, and used to leave the viewport blank: the
# load ran, but nothing asked for the full render it needed, so the loop only redrew the UI over the
# empty 3D layer painted mid-load. Compared as presented (PRESENTED), which is what shows that.
RenderEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
# Click "Open file..." on the message
MouseMoveEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
LeftButtonPressEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
LeftButtonReleaseEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 682 36 0 0 0 0 0
